From f9a621865334214a289c97cb541bc7dafe0d570e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Theorem Labs
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 21:45:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [sanitizer_common] intercept timer_create on musl
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

🤖: SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TIMER_CREATE is SI_GLIBC in llvmorg-20.1.8
(sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h:263), and no earlier patch of this
series changes it.  So on musl the runtime has no interceptor of
timer_create, timer_delete, timer_gettime or timer_settime, and the wrap
list has none of these names.  A static musl program's calls of these
functions go straight to libc.  libc writes *timer, *curr_value and
*old_value in code that ASan does not instrument, so ASan checks none of
these writes.

The TODO above the gate keeps it at glibc until someone checks the
timer_t typedefs of other platforms.  For musl f21a9653 these checks pass:

- include/time.h:110-113 declares timer_create, timer_delete,
  timer_settime and timer_gettime with glibc's prototypes.
- musl's timer_t is void * (include/alltypes.h.in:40).
  __sanitizer_timer_t is void * on Linux too
  (sanitizer_platform_limits_posix.h:1535).
- sizeof(struct itimerspec) is 32 on x86_64, aarch64, riscv64 and armv7.
  musl's struct timespec has a 64-bit tv_sec on all four targets, and it
  pads the long tv_nsec to 64 bits (include/alltypes.h.in:44).  Patch
  0008 gives __sanitizer_timespec the same layout on 32-bit musl, so
  sizeof(__sanitizer_itimerspec) is 32 too.  The build test of this
  toolchain asserts the libc side with a _Static_assert, because a test
  program cannot name the runtime's type.

Check musl as well.  The gate holds four interceptors
(sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc:2292-2345).  The timer_create
interceptor checks the write of *timer when the call succeeds.
timer_gettime checks the write of *curr_value.  timer_settime checks the
read of *new_value and the write of *old_value.  timer_delete checks
nothing.  Outside glibc, COMMON_INTERCEPT_FUNCTION_GLIBC_VER_MIN is a
plain COMMON_INTERCEPT_FUNCTION (lines 324-326), so the "GLIBC_2.3.3"
version in INIT_TIMER_CREATE has no effect on musl.

On 32-bit Arm, musl's headers send calls of timer_gettime and
timer_settime to __timer_gettime64 and __timer_settime64
(include/time.h:154-155).  The renames at the top of
sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc (lines 164-232) already map these
names.  So on armv7 musl the runtime attaches the two interceptors under
__timer_gettime64 and __timer_settime64.  timer_create and timer_delete
keep their plain names on every target.

sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h is a shared header.  The runtimes of
this toolchain that include sanitizer_common_interceptors.inc and keep
this gate change: ASan (the archive and its wrap list), MSan (the archive
and its wrap list) and TSan.  HWASan sets the gate to 0 itself
(hwasan_platform_interceptors.h:203-204), and standalone UBSan does not
include the .inc.  MemProf also includes the .inc, but this toolchain
does not build MemProf.  A toolchain that has this patch is a new
toolchain version.  Its libclang_rt.asan.a is not the archive that the
earlier binaries linked.

Line numbers in this message are those of llvmorg-20.1.8 and of musl
f21a9653.
---
 .../lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h     | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h
index 04b2f2790..11914c9c0 100644
--- a/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h
+++ b/compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_platform_interceptors.h
@@ -264,7 +264,8 @@ SANITIZER_WEAK_IMPORT void *aligned_alloc(__sanitizer::usize __alignment,
   (SI_LINUX || SI_FREEBSD || SI_NETBSD)
 // TODO: This should be SI_POSIX, adding glibc first until I have time
 // to verify all timer_t typedefs on other platforms.
-#define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TIMER_CREATE SI_GLIBC
+// musl's timer_t is void *, as glibc's is, and its timer_* prototypes match.
+#define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TIMER_CREATE (SI_GLIBC || SANITIZER_MUSL)
 #define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_GETITIMER SI_POSIX
 #define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TIME SI_POSIX
 #define SANITIZER_INTERCEPT_TIMESPEC_GET SI_LINUX
